I've always hated responses which began with BZZZT or No, No, No....

_Technically_ speaking, the minimum number of wishes you can get is 0.
I think that Brajesh was trying to say that, if you knew what you were
doing, you could wrest at least 4 from any wand of wishing that wasn't
just a pile of dust.

Spoilers to follow:

Even if there were no charges on the wand, a *blessed* scroll of charging
will charge it with 3 wishes.  (Unless, perhaps you found it in a ghost
pile and the previous owner (who somehow managed to die...) had already
done so.)  Assuming that the charging worked you would get the 3 and then
you could zap and zap and zap until you got that *last* wish from the 
sucker and it turned to dust.  I can usually get no less than 5 from the
wow in the castle, if I have a magic marker and some holy water left and
have at least identified a scroll of charging some time in the game...

I didn't intend for this to become a boasting session, but...

My current priest has become one of those nethack characters which are
hard to buy Christmas presents for.  He was near death in a small treasure
zoo, when out of desperation, he zapped this wand in hopes of staving off
the inevitable a few turns.  Well the wand gave him a wish (3 in fact!)
and he soon had cleared out the room.  He's currently trying to locate 
the amulet on level 48.  His only weakness is that his hit points are under
100.  Most monsters don't take him below 60 anyway.  I suspect that he would
be an even match for the death-star with his current armaments.

